<article class="env-definition" id="06NV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06NV">Definition <span data-tag="06NV">8.10.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a fibred category. We say $(\mathcal{S}, \text{Cov}(\mathcal{S}))$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/06NU" data-tag="06NU">8.10.1</a> is the <em>structure of site on $\mathcal{S}$ inherited from $\mathcal{C}$</em>. We sometimes indicate this by saying that <em>$\mathcal{S}$ is endowed with the topology inherited from $\mathcal{C}$</em>. </p>
